			<div class="content" id="post-content-3683903">
									

<p>I think I agree with Kalinin in that the concept of &quot;portal to the infinite realm of [x]&quot; is starting to become a cliche in the wake of 3008's success. Not that it's isn't a fun idea; just that now because of that, the bar is going to be set much higher in regards to what gets accepted and what gets labeled a lack-luster example of the trope.</p>
<p>I also agree that, as far as logs go, this one's were a little on the boring side. The dialogue wasn't that bad, but there also wasn't anything particularly interesting about these D's that I haven't seen many times before, and I found myself accurately predicting what was going to happen pretty easily. The only thing I was surprised about was how long it took to find the chair-ified D-Class. Called that one as soon as he put the coat over himself after it was established that &quot;thing on top of other thing = chair&quot;.</p>
<p>All that said, I do like the novelty of the concept, and you did get a chuckle out of me in certain spots (the mental image of a herd of chairs galloping, mahogany chair made of smaller mahogany chairs). Novote for now, feel free to ping me if you polish it up any and I'll reconsider giving and upvote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
